are only vaccinated people allowed to  vote in germany  this claim about the federal election is  circulating on the net but this is not  true  vitw examined why  let's take a closer look this tweet says  people without a coveted vaccination  cannot vote in germany and are banned  from entering polling stations there is  even talk of electoral fraud  beatrix von steuch an mp from the far  right alternative for germany party  known as afd alleged that the federal  returning officer had also considered  banning unvaccinated people in a  response to his tweet  our unvaccinated people really denied  the right to vote  false  fact is unvaccinated people are allowed  to vote at the polling stations like  everyone else if they observe the  applicable hygiene measures  they can also vote by post  voters have the right to cast their  ballots regardless of their vaccination  status confirms the federal returning  officer to the w  is  [Music]  more than 60 million eligible voters  will be able to elect a new parliament  this year  many germans have one concern  can the election be manipulated through  disinformation  82 percent fear exactly that according  to a survey and more than every second  person has stumbled across politically  motivated fake news online  what can you do about it we will show  you some fakes and also how to recognize  them  let's take the examples of election  posters  they are currently hanging all over  germany but not all of them are real  this one says everyone is talking about  the climate  we are ruining it  a clear fake the cdo confirmed the  poster is not theirs extension rebellion  a group of environmental activists  confirmed that it's their work  this is a special form of so-called  negative campaigning the attempt to  defame political opponents  even if they're meant to be satirical  some might consider the posters to be  genuine  some fake election posters also target  top politicians  cdu's chancellor candidate amin lachet  is misquoted here  flood i can only laugh about that  that's a fake  noise  [Music]  these posters were hanging in some major  german cities and intended to ridicule  the greens and their goals  the greens made it clear it is a fake  both the cdu and the greens party  suspect these are smear campaigns by  political parties like the far right afd  such campaigns often see the false  posters circulate on social media with  some even going viral  most attacks take place digitally and  the greens are particularly affected in  the german election  according to an investigation by the ngo  avas their chancellor candidate analina  bayabak  some of the misinformation circulating  online says that bayabok is planning to  terminate widow pension in order to  accommodate migrants  or this bizarre one that she would ban  pets because they emit carbon dioxide  these are false  bearbach never claimed such things such  claims are not listed in the green's  election manifesto either  amin lashed from the conservative cdu  experienced another political hit he was  wrongly accused of sifting off donations  for germany's flood victims toward his  own election campaign  this claim is also unsubstantiated and  false  the money collected from the donations  has already been partially paid out to  the flood victims  we hardly found any disinformation on  olaf schultz or his party the spd  however some fakes are also directed  against the election itself especially  the postal vote a record number of  postal ballots are expected this year  due to the pandemic  some claim the postal vote is easy to  manipulate  and that someone could also cast a  ballot using the names of dead people  does that sound familiar to you  donald trump and the republicans use  similar rhetoric in the 2020 u.s  presidential election but today there is  no evidence of systemic manipulation of  postal voting  and in germany can postal votes be  easily manipulated  misleading  when voting by post nobody can guarantee  that a voter cast their vote without any  influence from third parties  however the postal ballot itself is  protected against misuse through several  measures  have you come across fakes lately  what should we take a closer look at  next time  let us know in the comments below or by  mail at factchecking dw.com  you
 

